/-! ## §4 — Gate-1 arithmetic at `c = 10` -/

/-- **Gate-1 arithmetic at `c = 10` under the hybrid scheme.**

States the COMPUTED gate value `0.98497142`, not the fixed `3/4` of the
old `Mc_lb = 1/8` shape. That fixed target is false from `c = 29/4` on (here the
margin against it is `-0.23497142`), while the parameterised criterion
`L0(c−r)·r < Mc_lb` holds far beyond it — so the bound must be the real one. -/
theorem gate1_arithmetic_hybrid {epsOm : ℝ} (hEps : epsOm ≤ 1 / 10 ^ 21) :
    (100 : ℝ) * ((1557877851/160000000000 : ℝ) + 7 / 10 ^ 7 + 12 / 10 ^ 8 + epsOm)
      + (10 : ℝ) * ((358641871/320000000000 : ℝ) + 7 / 10 ^ 7 + 12 / 10 ^ 8 + epsOm)
      ≤ 98497141534375000011/100000000000000000000 := by
  nlinarith [hEps]

end

